{"term":"pivot","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:cbcdbcf173d271fd2e","definition":"A thing on which something turns; specifically a metal pointed pin or short shaft in machinery, such as the end of an axle or spindle.","example":"The weight of the body and the traction and braking forces are taken by the conventional dished bogie centre pivot with phosphor-bronze liner; this type of centre pivot facilitates passage over marshalling yard humps.","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["emotional pivot","pivot bridge","pivot gearing","pivot gun","pivotless","pivotlike","pivot man","pivot operation","pivot pin","pivot point","pivot tooth"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pivot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:81aaa813e7d28ad70c","definition":"Something or someone having a paramount significance in a certain situation.","example":"“The story of this adoption is, of course, the pivot round which all the circumstances of the mysterious tragedy revolved. Mrs. Yule had an only son, namely, William, to whom she was passionately attached ; but, like many a fond mother, she had the desire of mapping out that son's future entirely according to her own ideas.[…]”","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"broadly, figuratively","register":"broadly, figuratively","wordFamily":["emotional pivot","pivot bridge","pivot gearing","pivot gun","pivotless","pivotlike","pivot man","pivot operation","pivot pin","pivot point","pivot tooth"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pivot#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:23921519a87881c03c","definition":"Act of turning on one foot.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily"